publicizing the schools general harassment policy rather than banning
computer material.]

Newsgroups: comp.admin.policy,alt.comp.acad-freedom.talk
From: kadie@cs.uiuc.edu (Carl M Kadie)
Subject:  Re: University computers and pornography
Message-ID: <CLLt0B.1uu@cs.uiuc.edu>
Date: Tue, 22 Feb 1994 02:16:58 GMT

What is Stanford's policy w.r.t. to pornography in the library?  in
student newspapers? I can't think of any good reason why computer
media should be treated differently than traditional media.

Here at U. of Illinois a committee did look at a similar issue. It's
recommendation was to publicize in the public computer labs the
University's general sexual harassment policy, but not to create any
new rules that singled out computer media or computer labs. (see
refs).

